course: dictionary
lesson: 8739
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Serpent is a noun with three main meanings: a snake, a monster in stories, and an old word for a sly, tricky person. To pick the right one, read the whole sentence and look for clues.
explain: «The serpent persuaded Eve that God was keeping something good from her.» The serpent here is a creature that tricks someone, so the clues point to a sly, tricky character. The word is being used for a creature in a story, not a plain animal.
explain: «Alice is called a «serpent» by the Pigeon because of her long neck.» The clue is the long neck. The Pigeon is comparing Alice to a snake, so the meaning is a snake-like creature. Ask yourself: is it a real animal, a monster in a story, or a sly person? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A serpent is a snake, especially a big one. In science lessons we say «snake».
fact: In myths and stories, a serpent can be a huge snake-like monster, such as a sea serpent.
fact: «Serpent» can also mean a sly, tricky person who cannot be trusted. This is an old use of the word.
fact: Snakes do eat birds' eggs, so the Pigeon's fear in the story is real for birds.
fact: The plural of serpent is serpents. Phrases include «sea serpent» and «a serpent's tongue».
exercise: «The fisherman saw a sea serpent rising from the waves.» What is a sea serpent here? | A bird with long legs | *A huge snake-like monster from myths | A small fish | A ship's sail
exercise: Grandad says the new man is a serpent, sly and not to be trusted. What does serpent mean here? | A kind of tall tree | A famous sea monster | *A sly, tricky person who cannot be trusted | A green garden snake
exercise: Which word is the plural of serpent? | serpentine | serpent's | serpentes | *serpents
test: «The serpent persuaded Eve that God was keeping something good from her.» What does serpent mean in this story? | A kind of bird | *A sly creature that tricks Eve | A tall tree in the garden | A sea monster that sinks ships
test: What does the phrase «sea serpent» mean? | *A huge snake-like monster in stories | A ship with a snake painted on it | A type of fish | A song sung on boats
exam: Jayden says serpent is always a real animal. Is he right? | Yes, it always means a real animal | Yes, but only a sea animal | *No, it can mean a snake, a monster in stories, or a sly person | No, it is a type of tree
